---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/docs/CodeBlock.astro'
import Callout from '../../../components/docs/Callout.astro'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="<attestto-sign> Component"
  description="Sign documents with any DID wallet using the attestto-sign Web Component. Produces W3C Verifiable Credentials."
  currentPath="/docs/verify/sign-component/"
>
  <h1>&lt;attestto-sign&gt;</h1>
  <p class="docs-hero-sub">
    Sign documents with any DID wallet. The output is a Verifiable Credential,
    not a modified file &mdash; the original document is never altered.
  </p>

  <h2>Basic usage</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="HTML">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-tag">&lt;script</span> <span class="c-attr">type</span>=<span class="c-str">"module"</span>
  <span class="c-attr">src</span>=<span class="c-str">"https://unpkg.com/@attestto/verify"</span>
<span class="c-tag">&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</span>

<span class="c-tag">&lt;attestto-sign&gt;&lt;/attestto-sign&gt;</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    The sign component uses <a href="/docs/wallets/">@attestto/id-wallet-adapter</a> under the hood to
    discover and connect to DID wallets. The signing flow follows five steps:
  </p>

  <div class="docs-steps">
    <div class="docs-step">
      <div class="docs-step-num">1</div>
      <div class="docs-step-body">
        <p><strong>Discover wallets</strong> &mdash; Scans for available DID wallets using the wallet adapter's discovery protocol (browser extensions, mobile deep links, CHAPI).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-step">
      <div class="docs-step-num">2</div>
      <div class="docs-step-body">
        <p><strong>Select wallet</strong> &mdash; The user picks their wallet from the built-in picker. The component connects and retrieves the user's DID.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-step">
      <div class="docs-step-num">3</div>
      <div class="docs-step-body">
        <p><strong>Drop PDF</strong> &mdash; The user drops or selects a document. The component computes its SHA-256 hash locally.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-step">
      <div class="docs-step-num">4</div>
      <div class="docs-step-body">
        <p><strong>Sign</strong> &mdash; The hash (not the document) is sent to the wallet for signing. The wallet prompts the user for approval and returns a cryptographic signature.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-step">
      <div class="docs-step-num">5</div>
      <div class="docs-step-body">
        <p><strong>Store</strong> &mdash; The signed Verifiable Credential is stored in the user's wallet. It can be presented to any verifier later.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Callout type="info">
    <strong>Output is a Verifiable Credential.</strong> The component does not modify the original PDF
    or produce a signed file download. Instead, it creates a W3C Verifiable Credential that binds the
    signer's DID to the document hash. The VC is stored in the user's identity wallet.
  </Callout>

  <h2>Attributes</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Attribute</th>
        <th>Type</th>
        <th>Default</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>theme</code></td>
        <td><code>"light" | "dark"</code></td>
        <td><code>"light"</code></td>
        <td>Color scheme for the component.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>wallet-filter</code></td>
        <td><code>string</code></td>
        <td>&mdash;</td>
        <td>Comma-separated list of wallet IDs to show. Omit to show all discovered wallets.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>credential-type</code></td>
        <td><code>string</code></td>
        <td><code>"DocumentSignature"</code></td>
        <td>The Verifiable Credential type to issue.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Events</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Event</th>
        <th>Detail</th>
        <th>When</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>wallet-connected</code></td>
        <td><code>&#123; did: string, walletId: string &#125;</code></td>
        <td>A wallet has been selected and connected.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>sign-started</code></td>
        <td><code>&#123; fileName: string, hash: string, did: string &#125;</code></td>
        <td>The user has approved signing and the operation has begun.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>sign-complete</code></td>
        <td><code>&#123; credential: object, hash: string, did: string &#125;</code></td>
        <td>Signing succeeded. The credential is a full W3C Verifiable Credential.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>sign-error</code></td>
        <td><code>&#123; error: string, code: string &#125;</code></td>
        <td>Signing failed (wallet rejected, timeout, etc.).</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Event handling</h3>

  <CodeBlock lang="JavaScript">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">const</span> signer = document.<span class="c-fn">querySelector</span>(<span class="c-str">'attestto-sign'</span>)

signer.<span class="c-fn">addEventListener</span>(<span class="c-str">'wallet-connected'</span>, (e) <span class="c-op">=&gt;</span> <span class="c-br">{</span>
  console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(<span class="c-str">'Connected DID:'</span>, e.detail.did)
<span class="c-br">}</span>)

signer.<span class="c-fn">addEventListener</span>(<span class="c-str">'sign-complete'</span>, (e) <span class="c-op">=&gt;</span> <span class="c-br">{</span>
  console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(<span class="c-str">'Signed by:'</span>, e.detail.did)
  console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(<span class="c-str">'Document hash:'</span>, e.detail.hash)
  console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(<span class="c-str">'Credential:'</span>, e.detail.credential)

  <span class="c-cm">// The VC is already stored in the wallet.</span>
  <span class="c-cm">// You can also record it on your backend:</span>
  <span class="c-fn">fetch</span>(<span class="c-str">'/api/signatures'</span>, <span class="c-br">{</span>
    method: <span class="c-str">'POST'</span>,
    body: JSON.<span class="c-fn">stringify</span>(e.detail)
  <span class="c-br">}</span>)
<span class="c-br">}</span>)

signer.<span class="c-fn">addEventListener</span>(<span class="c-str">'sign-error'</span>, (e) <span class="c-op">=&gt;</span> <span class="c-br">{</span>
  console.<span class="c-fn">error</span>(<span class="c-str">'Sign failed:'</span>, e.detail.error)
<span class="c-br">}</span>)`} />
  </CodeBlock>

